# UCDMS prompts

Before changing login, add-lead, or edit automation, read `prompts/PROMPTS.md`.

- Add lead: `npm test` is login + all add cases; never include edit. One happy-path add is `npm run test:add`. Combined add → edit → stock is `npm run test:flow` (edit and stock still use the Chrome pickers).
- Edit: `npm run test:edit`. User picks the lead in Chrome. Never open the top row unless they chose that ID.
- My Stock: `npm run test:stock`. User picks the exact INV ID in a Chrome overlay picker (list / type / refresh / cancel), same as edit. Update enabled fields only; never alter read-only data to force certification. If listing_price is 0, override a non-zero price and confirm it on getlead before Ready For Sale.
- Stock images: upload Images-tab photos only when certification type is JLR Approved. Skip them for Non-Certified and on dms.jlr.local. Fill the Certification Checklist with Yes only for JLR Approved; leave it unanswered for Non-Certified.
- Edit login: reuse `test-results/auth/dealer.json` only when it matches the current DMS_URL host. Changing local / stage / UAT forces a new captcha + OTP login. DEV captcha comes from data_optional; UAT/stage captcha is read from the image.
- JLR VIN: 17 chars, starts with SA, from `master_jlr_total_vins` via `getJlrVin`. Fill chassis last on add; if the API returns nothing, fail — do not submit an empty VIN.
- Evaluation: if Latest Evaluation Details popup appears, click OK and continue. Skip the checklist only when already completed (evaluation_done = y / Completed badge / read-only). Otherwise randomly all OK, all Not OK, or mixed. Sub-options/remarks are per-option config, so fill them for OK too. Random Ref. Exp amount on a random subset of questions, never overwriting an existing one. No question-image uploads.
- Images tab: skip uploads on dms.jlr.local. Elsewhere upload only mandatory cards (red *), skip ones already filled, one at a time with DMS_UPLOAD_DELAY_MS pacing — stage rate-limits (429) and blocks for minutes. Confirm from the API response, never from networkidle.
- Status of Lead for evaluation: Follow up + Evaluation Scheduled, then Lead Classification, Evaluation Place, follow-up date, remarks.
- After evaluation is complete, move the lead one status at a time up to Purchased (Follow up → Deal Done → Purchased). If the lead is already Deal Done, skip Evaluation and still go to Purchased. Deal Done needs evaluation_done = y; Purchased needs pricing, Exchange, mandatory Purchase files (Price Agreement always; RC when the field shows *), and the 22 mandatory Images-tab photos — upload any that are missing before the Purchased update.
- Stock certification: JLR only (`is_certifiable` and `is_brand_group` must both be y), no Not OK post-refurbishment answers, Refurbishment Not Done must be false, age < 5 years, mileage < 125000 km. Stop if the two make flags disagree. Skip Demo Section, fill rendered dependents, and do not upload question images. When post-refurbishment is already completed, skip it and open Certification — do not wait for status 2; getlead can stay at 1. After Confirm, click Yes on the Non-Certified / JLR Approved `$confirmToast` (`button.btn-ok`) so savecertification runs and status becomes Ready For Sale. Finish and API-confirm inventory status 3 (Ready For Sale): non-JLR goes there after refurbishment; JLR goes through certification, using Non-Certified when any criterion fails.
